   "sentenceId": 15,
   "he": "בְּאַנְפִּילְיָא חֲלִיצָתָהּ פְּסוּלָה כּוּ׳. לְמֵימְרָא דְּאַנְפִּילְיָא לָאו מִנְעָל הוּא?",
   "en": "The Gemara analyzes the phrase used in the mishna that discusses the types of shoes that can be used for ḥalitza. It was taught in the mishna that if he was wearing «a soft shoe [anpileya]» made of cloth for ḥalitza, «her ḥalitza is invalid.» The Gemara explains: «That is to say that an anpileya is not» considered «a shoe.»"
  }
